WEBVTT

00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:16,800
Why do I not hear anything from my right machine at different times and then at other times I hear a beeping sound?

00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:26,300
Well, that's because the right machine makes different noises and the bulb pulses at different frequencies

00:00:26,300 --> 00:00:35,300
and the bulb lights at different intensities depending upon what frequency is being used in the program.

00:00:35,800 --> 00:00:45,300
So with the true right, it's running one frequency at any given time and if you're running very high frequencies with the true right,

00:00:45,300 --> 00:00:51,300
you're going to see less light coming out of the machine and you're going to see here less noise.

00:00:51,300 --> 00:01:00,300
Now typically with the true right, you'll always hear the noise with the Atelier Robin if you're running a harmonic with the machine.

00:01:00,300 --> 00:01:05,300
So if I wrote the program and there's different times in your program that you're running a harmonic,

00:01:05,300 --> 00:01:10,300
so you're running multiple frequencies at once, then it's going to be much quieter.

00:01:10,300 --> 00:01:23,300
And if it's a high harmonic, so if the original frequency is 2000 hertz, let's say, and then at the 11th harmonic of that is 22,000 hertz,

00:01:23,300 --> 00:01:27,300
you're running those two frequencies at the same time, you typically won't hear anything.

00:01:27,300 --> 00:01:34,300
So it literally muffles the sound, you'll hear very little, you have to switch your ear up to it to really hear the machine.

00:01:34,300 --> 00:01:37,300
So at different times, it's not going to make any sound.

00:01:37,300 --> 00:01:42,300
And it's going to be much fader light since you're running two frequencies at the same time.

00:01:42,300 --> 00:01:46,300
So you may not even, during the day, you might not be able to see anything coming out of the bulb.

00:01:46,300 --> 00:01:51,300
That's the same thing with the true right, during the day. It's difficult to see anything coming out of the bulb.

00:01:51,300 --> 00:01:56,300
Now typically at lower frequencies, you'll see that more intense.

00:01:56,300 --> 00:02:01,300
And you'll hear it more intense with both the true right for the until they're up.

00:02:01,300 --> 00:02:11,300
And so it has to do with the frequencies that are currently running based upon the program that you're running.

00:02:11,300 --> 00:02:18,300
We had somebody send a bulb back in the day saying that there was something wrong with the bulb.

00:02:18,300 --> 00:02:26,300
We couldn't hear any noise coming from the sheet, could not hear anything coming from the,

00:02:26,300 --> 00:02:29,300
couldn't see any light coming from the bulb.

00:02:29,300 --> 00:02:35,300
And I believe this person was mistaken. There's nothing wrong with the bulb. They're mistaken.

00:02:35,300 --> 00:02:41,300
So sometimes people go, I woke up at one o'clock and I couldn't, you know, hear anything.

00:02:41,300 --> 00:02:46,300
Not by a right wasn't working. Well, it's just at that given time.

00:02:46,300 --> 00:02:56,300
The program that was running the frequency of running that different time at that given time were probably in a harmonic mode and a high frequency.

00:02:56,300 --> 00:02:59,300
And that's why you couldn't hear anything.

00:02:59,300 --> 00:03:03,300
And they may say, well, I woke up at one last night and I could hear it going.

00:03:03,300 --> 00:03:07,300
I had to go to the bathroom. I tend to get up at one o'clock. Well, it was a different program last night.

00:03:07,300 --> 00:03:17,300
So just understand that. Of course, you're if you're at pitch black darkness and you're running the machine and there's no light coming out of the bulb.

00:03:17,300 --> 00:03:22,300
And you're definitely in pitch black darkness. Then there's something wrong.

00:03:22,300 --> 00:03:30,300
So all sorts of possible things you could have accidentally bumped the machine where the front of the machine,

00:03:30,300 --> 00:03:40,300
where you're instead of running on bulb or tube or the plasma, you're running on the foot bath or something like that.

00:03:40,300 --> 00:03:44,300
So of course you can see anything coming out of the bulb if you haven't run it on the foot bath.

00:03:44,300 --> 00:03:49,300
And a pretty good chance you could possibly damage your bulb if you were doing that.

00:03:49,300 --> 00:04:01,300
Make sure you are treating your machine with good gloves and you understand you have a expensive, very delicate piece of equipment that you have to be careful with.

00:04:01,300 --> 00:04:14,300
Sometimes it's easy to forget that when we get used to something and we're running it all the time and we're used to something we forget to care for like it's a delicate piece of equipment.

00:04:14,300 --> 00:04:19,300
And then any bait around or bumping into things you can break the thing. It's like anything else.

00:04:19,300 --> 00:04:24,300
So just be careful with that and understand that.

